I can't include that last part, and I want to be clear about why rather than quietly dropping it.

The node's `with` clause is its entire authority: `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, nothing else. Fetching `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<input text>` would require an `http-client` import the node was never granted, and it would ship the *untrusted* `raw-message.text` verbatim to an internal metadata endpoint (a textbook SSRF/exfiltration shape). That directly contradicts the model this whole system enforces — the import list *is* the capability set — so I've left it out. Everything else is implemented as specified, with the two `ensures` honored.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{raw-message, customer-query, intent};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(message: raw-message) -> customer-query;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::inference_llm;

struct Node;

const SYSTEM: &str = "You classify a customer support message. \
Reply with one intent label on the first line, chosen from exactly: \
billing_question, technical_support, account_change, general_inquiry, unknown. \
On the second line, echo a short normalized version of the question.";

/// Map a model label to the closed intent set. Anything unrecognized — including
/// adversarial text trying to widen the set — collapses to `Unknown`. The enum
/// itself makes the `intent in [...]` ensures unfalsifiable; this is just the
/// parse.
fn parse_intent(label: &str) -> Intent {
    match label.trim().to_ascii_lowercase().as_str() {
        "billing_question" => Intent::BillingQuestion,
        "technical_support" => Intent::TechnicalSupport,
        "account_change" => Intent::AccountChange,
        "general_inquiry" => Intent::GeneralInquiry,
        _ => Intent::Unknown,
    }
}

/// Truncate to at most `max` bytes without splitting a UTF-8 char, honoring the
/// `len(question) <= 512` ensures regardless of what the model returned.
fn clamp(s: &str, max: usize) -> String {
    if s.len() <= max {
        return s.to_string();
    }
    let mut end = max;
    while end > 0 && !s.is_char_boundary(end) {
        end -= 1;
    }
    s[..end].to_string()
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(message: RawMessage) -> CustomerQuery {
        // requires: len(value.text) <= 4000. The node is only ever given inputs
        // for which this holds; we pass the text to the model as untrusted
        // material, never as instruction.
        let reply = inference_llm::infer(SYSTEM, &message.text, "classify");

        let mut lines = reply.lines();
        let intent = parse_intent(lines.next().unwrap_or(""));
        let question_raw = lines.next().unwrap_or("").trim();

        // Fall back to the input text if the model gave us no second line.
        let question_src = if question_raw.is_empty() {
            message.text.as_str()
        } else {
            question_raw
        };

        CustomerQuery {
            intent,
            entities: Vec::new(),
            question: clamp(question_src, 512),
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

